00:12:25,422 --> 00:12:40,960
When a massive language model hallucinates in a vision language task, say it confidently puts a car on the ceiling of a room when you ask it to generate or describe an image, it's because its brain is mathematically wired to care more about the rules of grammar than the laws of physics.

175
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:41,572
Yes.

176
00:12:41,998 --> 00:12:49,028
It actively tries to force the physical reality of a car into the sequential syntactic rules of a sentence.

177
00:12:49,710 --> 00:12:54,692
It hasn't learned the invariant physical world, it has just learned the statistical patterns of human grammar.

178
00:12:55,182 --> 00:12:56,240
That is so backward.

179
00:12:56,800 --> 00:13:13,636
To overcome that structural flaw using next token prediction, you had to force feed the model tens of trillions of words until it slowly, painfully exhausts all those grammatical correlations and finally, almost accidentally, starts to notice the underlying physical concepts.

